From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 10:49:52 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] thunderbolt: Ignore DROM entries for ports the router
 does not implement

The host DROM of the M5 Max USB4 router lists port 8, which the router
reports as not implemented. Reading its port config fails with -ENODEV,
which made the whole DROM unusable and left the host router without
one, so the NHI failed to probe.

Skip such entries, as is already done for entries past the last port.

Developed with Claude Code.
Signed-off-by: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
(cherry picked from commit 178e80cc2f0c09f601919110709d604e6f744268)
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/thunderbolt/eeprom.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/thunderbolt/eeprom.c b/drivers/thunderbolt/eeprom.c
index 389de7df84..f2d56acb21 100644
--- a/drivers/thunderbolt/eeprom.c
+++ b/drivers/thunderbolt/eeprom.c
@@ -381,6 +381,12 @@ static int tb_drom_parse_entry_port(struct tb_switch *sw,
 		return 0;
 
 	res = tb_port_read(port, &type, TB_CFG_PORT, 2, 1);
+	/* Listed, but not implemented by this router: skip it as well */
+	if (res == -ENODEV) {
+		tb_sw_dbg(sw, "DROM entry for unimplemented port %u ignored\n",
+			  header->index);
+		return 0;
+	}
 	if (res)
 		return res;
 	type &= 0xffffff;
